.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="plot_graphene_dirac_cone looks at graphene&#x27;s bulk Bloch spectrum -- a linear Dirac cone with no gap. Cutting a finite flake out of the honeycomb lattice along its two primitive-lattice directions produces the classic &quot;zigzag&quot; edge termination, and with it a macroscopically degenerate band of zero-energy states with no bulk counterpart, localized entirely on the flake&#x27;s boundary and almost entirely on a single sublattice. Unlike the SSH or Haldane edge states elsewhere in this gallery, these zero modes are not protected by a bulk topological invariant -- they are a purely geometric consequence of the zigzag edge cut, and vanish under an armchair termination instead.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/condensed/topology/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_graphene_zigzag_flake_thumb.png
